cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this repository, cite the commit SHA you used. There are no tagged
  releases yet, and the gate, the spec and the demos change between commits;
  CHANGELOG.md records the dated changes.
title: "security-data-that-works: a deductive OCSF field-mapping check and a public security-data spec"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "flying-coyote"
repository-code: "https://github.com/flying-coyote/security-data-that-works"
url: "https://securitydataworks.com"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A runnable check that flags type-crossing OCSF field mappings with an OWL
  reasoner (ELK via ROBOT) over a hand-authored D3FEND disjointness layer, with
  no machine-learning model in the loop, plus a public statement of what good
  looks like across five categories of security data and runnable demos of a
  tiered open security-data lakehouse and a four-layer data-health gate.
keywords:
  - OCSF
  - D3FEND
  - OWL
  - field mapping
  - detection engineering
  - data quality
  - security data lakehouse
  - Apache Iceberg
